Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_UBO_AHEAD (+ _LARGE, _STATS, _VERIFY): run a frame ahead (EDEN_NX2_FRAMES_AHEAD=1), the back's uniform binds read the split front's copies of the constant buffer pages, taken after each list batch's submit and each semaphore acquire, instead of guest memory the game already rewrites for the next frame; all off by default

Follows GrowingBlackBeans' EDEN_GBB_UBO_AHEAD (issue 21, 9 Nov: 0439's present-time copy moved
into the one-frame-ahead present hit its 4 MiB cap and missed most frames the back recorded).
Here the front copies at the binds and draw methods it parses, so every frame the back records
has its copies: 4 KiB pages, once per capture epoch (each DmaPusher::DispatchCalls and each
semaphore acquire, met at once or not), a page whose bytes did not change keeps its copy, sent
to the back in stream order (GpuSplit::DeferWords, which now takes Defer's flags: the batches
are FastDrawNeutral). GPU writes reach the copies through the hooks 0439 placed
(UboSnapshot::OnGpuWrite). Copies live in a pool of 1 MiB blocks that grows on demand up to
128 MiB and is freed when the split stops. Ranges up to 4 KiB are served (of a larger binding
the first 4 KiB are captured for them); larger ones (the 64 KiB indirectly read banks) with
EDEN_UP_UBO_AHEAD_LARGE=1. Binds the copies can't serve read guest memory as before, counted by
reason. EDEN_UP_UBO_AHEAD_STATS=1 logs three lines every 10 s; EDEN_UP_UBO_AHEAD_VERIFY=1
compares each bind's copy, and each texture handle word a full resolve reads, with guest memory
(with or without UBO_AHEAD). Off with EDEN_UP_L1056_BACK_MACROS=1. Not covered: texture and
sampler handles (VERIFY counts changed handle words), compute constant buffers.

